From: WorkBuddy <wb@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:20:00 +0800
Subject: [OHOS] bottom-crop fix: GetOhosReservedHeight returns {0,true} (page always full-height)

Turn off browser-controls shrink of the renderer size so the page lays out
full-height and the fixed bottom bar / dock is never cropped. The real
decision point is the content-layer GetOhosReservedHeight() (linked into the
CEF target libweb_engine); the chrome-layer DoBrowserControlsShrinkRendererSize
return-false change is ineffective because libweb_engine does not link the
chrome layer.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc
@@ -1043,6 +1043,6 @@ OhosReservedHeight GetOhosReservedHeight(RenderWidgetHostImpl* host) {
   // Once the controls have slid away the page lays out in their room too
   // (DoBrowserControlsShrinkRendererSize turns false, as on Android), so a
   // fixed element sized to the viewport reaches the bottom of the screen
   // and not where the controls' edge was. What stays covered stays off.
-  return {view->DoBrowserControlsShrinkRendererSize() ? controls : 0, true};
+  return {0, true};  // [鸿蒙Chrome] 关掉浏览器控件对渲染尺寸的收缩：页面恒满高、底栏固定条完整
 }
